            "text": "The two vectors $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{A}}$ and $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}$ are drawn from a common point and $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{C}}=\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{A}}+\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}},$ then angle\nbetween $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{A}}$ and $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}}$ is -\n(1) $90^{\\circ}$ if $\\mathrm{C}^{2}=\\mathrm{A}^{2}+\\mathrm{B}^{2}$\n(2) greater than $90^{\\circ}$ if $\\mathrm{C}^{2}<\\mathrm{A}^{2}+\\mathrm{B}^{2}$\n(3) greater than $90^{\\circ}$ if $\\mathrm{C}^{2}>\\mathrm{A}^{2}+\\mathrm{B}^{2}$\n(4) less than $90^{\\circ}$ if $\\mathrm{C}^{2}>\\mathrm{A}^{2}+\\mathrm{B}^{2}$\nCorrect options are -",
            "image": null
