      "title": "Errors of Measurement",
      "totalQuestions": 3,
      "questions": [
        {
          "_id": "67726d13c49e8ef28ee2b40b",
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "67726ce6d221dc77889e6416",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2024-04-15T19:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2024 (Memory Based Paper 3)",
              "title": "BITSAT 2024 (Memory Based Paper 3)"
            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "You measure two quantities as $A=1.0 \\mathrm{~m} \\pm 0.2 \\mathrm{~m}$, $B=2.0 \\mathrm{~m} \\pm 0.2 \\mathrm{~m}$. We should report correct value for $\\sqrt{A B}$ as",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "midHw",
              "text": "$1.4 \\mathrm{~m} \\pm 0.4 \\mathrm{~m}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "aWYBZ",
              "text": "$1.41 \\mathrm{~m} \\pm 0.15 \\mathrm{~m}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "AFRwY",
              "text": "$1.4 \\mathrm{~m} \\pm 0.3 \\mathrm{~m}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "3cZSo",
              "text": "$1.4 \\mathrm{~m} \\pm 0.2 \\mathrm{~m}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Given, $A=1.0 \\mathrm{~m} \\pm 0.2 \\mathrm{~m}, B=2.0 \\mathrm{~m} \\pm 0.2 \\mathrm{~m}$\nLet $Y=\\sqrt{A B}=\\sqrt{(1.0)(20)}=1.414 \\mathrm{~m}$\nRounding off to two significant digits\n$\\begin{aligned}\nY & =1.4 \\mathrm{~m} \\\\\n\\frac{\\Delta Y}{Y} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\frac{\\Delta A}{A}+\\frac{\\Delta B}{B}\\right] \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\frac{0.2}{1.0}+\\frac{0.2}{2.0}\\right] \\\\\n& =\\frac{0.6}{2 \\times 20} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow \\quad \\Delta Y & =\\frac{0.6 Y}{2 \\times 20}=\\frac{0.6 \\times 1.4}{2 \\times 20}=0.212\n\\end{aligned}$\nRounding off to one significant digit,\n$\\Delta Y=0.2 \\mathrm{~m}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
          "previousYear": {
            "_id": "67726ce6d221dc77889e6416",
